How to Contribute
-----------------

libfyvterm is a hard fork. Bug reports, feature requests and patches for it
belong here:

    https://github.com/pantoniou/libfyvterm

Please do not send them to the original libvterm's author or to Neovim: this
tree has diverged from both. See PROVENANCE.md for what it took from each and
where the fork's own history begins.

Before starting on anything substantial, open an issue to discuss it. That
avoids duplicating work already in progress and settles design questions
before code is written.

For a change to the terminal's behaviour, add or update a test script under
t/. The suite is the only thing that makes a change to a 2000-line state
machine reviewable: each script interleaves harness commands with the
callback events they should produce, and CTest runs one case per file.

    cmake -S . -B build
    cmake --build build -j
    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

The build is warning-clean under -Wall -Wextra with gcc and clang, in Debug
and Release, with and without -DENABLE_ASAN=ON. Please keep it that way.

If you are porting a fix from Neovim's src/nvim/vterm, cite the upstream
commit in both the commit message and a comment at the change site, and add
it to the list in PROVENANCE.md, as the existing entries do.
